<br/>
<br/>General priority is making sure you have 1742 hit and that you wear leather in every slot. The latter is because of a passive that increases our intellect by 5% when we are only wearing leather. Beyond this you want to always make sure you use the highest possible ilvl in every slot, except for pvp gear which is notably weaker in pve. Trinkets are also a bit different, check trinket section for recommendations. Every item listed can be substituted for the normal version of the same item, but you might have to reforge for more hit.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="reforging">Reforging for Balance Druid DPS</h3>A new addition in Cataclysm is the ability to reforge. You can change some of one secondary stat to another, for example changing some hit into haste if you are over the hit cap. You can not change to a stat that is already on the item, for example an item with hit and haste can not have its hit changed to haste, but it can be  changed to mastery or crit. The easiest way to do reforging will be to download the addon Reforgelite Classic and input the stat weights 4.1 on hit, 2.1 on haste, 1.95 on mastery and 1.9 on crit, with hit cap of 1742. Leave spirit at 0 as default settings convert spirit to hit. This will calculate and auto reforge your gear in a way that gets you as close to your hit cap as possible and then maximizes your haste, and  then mastery. If you want to do it without addon just follow the same rules, get hit as close to 1742 as you can then maximize haste and then mastery.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="haste-breakpoints">Haste Breakpoints</h3>
<b>Note: Regardless of haste breakpoints, haste is always stronger than mastery and crit.</b>
<br/>At certain haste breakpoints, we get 1 more tick per cast of our dots. These breakpoints will be worth gearing towards if you are close to reaching one. Use of sims have found it to be worth sacrificing as much as 100 int for 100 haste by regemming for a breakpoint. The bis lists are keeping these breakpoints in mind, but when you are working towards them then it can take a lot of manual work to find the needed rating. The table below will display the rating needed for each extra tick.<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
